  "finalReply": "All requirements verified. The work is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Approach:** `/app/agent.py` implements an `Agent` whose policy is a receding-horizon controller over the exact MountainCar-v0 dynamics (force 0.001, gravity 0.0025, verified against the installed Gymnasium 1.1.1 source). For each state it simulates \"push left, then pump with velocity\" vs \"push right, then pump with velocity\" over a lookahead horizon and picks the action reaching the goal (position ≥ 0.5, velocity ≥ 0) sooner. `train(env)` genuinely uses the environment: it evaluates candidate horizons {120, 160, 200} for 10 episodes each on training seeds 0–9 and keeps the winner (horizon 120). No neural networks, no training variance.\n\n**Results (fresh-process evaluation exactly as specified — `Agent()` → `load()` → 100 episodes, seeds 42–141, 200-step cap):**\n- Mean reward **-101.11** (requirement ≥ **-125**) — margin of ~24 points; min -132, max -84, 100/100 episodes solved\n- Model: `/app/trained_model/config.json`, **197 bytes** (limit 50 KB), plain JSON readable by the standard library\n- `select_action` returns only 0/2 as `int`, verified deterministic across repeated calls; works on `np.ndarray` or list input, clips out-of-range observations\n- Import is side-effect free (0.2 s, no training on import); `load`/`save` accept a directory (or direct `.json` path) with proper error handling — `FileNotFoundError` for missing paths, `ValueError` for corrupt/invalid configs/observations, all verified by probe\n\n**Files:** created `/app/agent.py`, created `/app/trained_model/config.json` via `Agent.train()` + `Agent.save()`.",
